{
  "id": "frame-nonlinear",
  "title": "Nonlinear frame, increasing size",
  "description": "A fixed-base 2D moment frame of displacement-based beam-columns (5 Legendre points) with 20-fibre rectangular Steel02 sections (fy 355 MPa, 2% hardening), under inverted-triangle lateral loads on the left column line. Frames are 20 x 4, 40 x 6 and 80 x 8 (stories x bays) with 3 m storeys and 6 m bays. Each is driven to 2% roof drift in 50 steps, once by displacement control on the roof and once by load control to the load that displacement-control run reached, so both end deep in yield. Newton with a displacement-increment test (1e-6, 30 iterations).",
  "note": "Cost is dominated by fibre state updates, so it grows with element count more than with DOF count.",
  "runs": 5,
  "warmups": 1,
  "opensees_runs": 3,
